# Hard no-CGO requirement

- Production Mew binaries must build and run with `CGO_ENABLED=0`.
- Do not add dependencies that require CGO for functionality used by Mew.
- A dependency is acceptable only if the used production path has a complete no-CGO implementation.
- Do not introduce required C, C++, Rust FFI, system-library bindings, dynamically linked native libraries, or platform SDK bindings that depend on CGO.
- Do not rely on optional native acceleration when disabling it changes required correctness or compatibility.
- All production builds, normal builds, release builds, conformance jobs, cross-builds, and non-race tests must explicitly use `CGO_ENABLED=0`.
- Race jobs are the only permitted exception because the Go race detector may require CGO.
- Race-only CGO must not become a production dependency.
- Preserve no-CGO cross-compilation for every supported Linux, macOS, and Windows target.
- Reject a proposed dependency if it cannot satisfy the no-CGO requirement.
<!-- MEW-NO-CGO_END -->
